      "og:site_name": "SocialAPI"
    }
  },
  "markdown": {
    "instructions": [
      "Base URL: https://api.social-api.ai/v1. Send your API key in the Authorization header: Authorization: Bearer <your API key>.",
      "Every error response from /v1 is JSON: { \"error\": { \"code\", \"message\", \"meta\" (optional) }, \"request_id\" }. Branch on error.code; use error.message only for logs.",
      "A 429 response carries a Retry-After header, in seconds, when the limit has a known wait. Authenticated responses can carry X-RateLimit-Limit, X-RateLimit-Remaining, and X-RateLimit-Reset for the per-minute request budget your SocialAPI account shares across every API key (see /guides/rate-limits).",
      "Paginated list endpoints return next_cursor, at the top level or inside pagination (see /guides/pagination). Pass it as the cursor query parameter to get the next page. An absent or empty next_cursor means you have the last page.",
      "Treat every ID as an opaque string: do not parse it or assume a format.",
      "Support differs by platform and by operation. Check /platforms/overview before assuming an operation works on a platform. An unsupported operation returns 501 with error.code resource.not_supported."
    ]
  },
  "api": {
    "examples": {
      "languages": ["bash", "javascript", "python"]
    }
  },
